--TEST--
A write through `Core\Reflect\ClassInfo::set` reaches the same `PropertyObserver` an ordinary write reaches, and a throwing observer fails it the same way — `rule:security/reflection-enforces-visibility`, `rule:classes/property-observer-pipeline`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Reflect\ClassInfo::set
// `rule:security/reflection-enforces-visibility`: acting on a reflected property runs the `PropertyObserver`
// hook ordinary code at that call site would face. This asks that as an
// agreement rather than as a sentence — the same write through both doors,
// with the observer saying which door it was told about being impossible,
// because it is told the same thing either way.
class Ledger implements PropertyObserver {
    public int $balance = 0;

    public function onPropertyGet(string $name, mixed $value): void {
    }

    public function onPropertySet(string $name, mixed $value): void {
        echo "  set ", $name, " = ", $value, "\n";
        Tally::$writes = Tally::$writes + 1;
    }
}

final class Tally {
    public static int $writes = 0;
}

Ledger $book = new Ledger();
var $described = Core\Reflect::forObject($book);

echo "ordinary:\n";
$book->balance = 7;

echo "reflective:\n";
$described->set($book, "balance", 7);

// `rule:classes/property-observer-pipeline`: the observer is told the value that was *committed*, which is
// what a following read answers — so the line above is a report of a store and
// not a report instead of one.
echo "stored ", $described->get($book, "balance"), "\n";

// § 4: a class that implements nothing pays nothing, through either door.
final class Plain {
    public int $n = 0;
}
Plain $p = new Plain();
var $flat = Core\Reflect::forObject($p);
echo "a class that implements nothing:\n";
$p->n = 99;
$flat->set($p, "n", 99);

// § 3: "a throwing `onPropertySet` still fails the overall write", and a
// reflective write is not the place that changes.
final class Fussy implements PropertyObserver {
    public int $n = 0;

    public function onPropertyGet(string $name, mixed $value): void {
    }

    public function onPropertySet(string $name, mixed $value): void {
        throw new LogicError("refusing " . $name);
    }
}
Fussy $f = new Fussy();
var $strict = Core\Reflect::forObject($f);
try {
    $strict->set($f, "n", 1);
    echo "unreachable\n";
} catch (LogicError $thrown) {
    echo "caught ", $thrown->message, "\n";
}

// The count is the invariant, not any one line above it: two writes on an
// observing class, one per door, and the class that implements nothing added
// neither.
echo "writes=", Tally::$writes, "\n";
--EXPECT--
ordinary:
  set balance = 7
reflective:
  set balance = 7
stored 7
a class that implements nothing:
caught refusing n
writes=2
